From: kschen <admin@kschen.eu.org>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 00:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ASoC: tfa989x: add support for TFA9891

The Xiaomi Mi 5s (msm8996pro-xiaomi-capricorn) carries an amplifier that
the downstream device tree calls "tfa,tfa9890", but which reports
revision 0x92 rather than the 0x80 the TFA9890 entry expects:

  tfa989x 1-0034: invalid revision number, expected 0x80, got 0x92

The downstream tfa98xx driver does not trust the compatible either - it
distinguishes the various TFA1 parts by reading the revision register at
runtime, and its firmware container list includes tfa9891 alongside
tfa9890.  Revision 0x92 is TFA9891.

TFA9891 is register compatible with TFA9890 for everything this driver
touches.  Verified on capricorn by forcing the TFA9890 entry to accept
0x92: the I2C reset, the tfa9890 init sequence (unhide key, PLL bits at
0x59, re-hide, CURRENTSENSE2) and the DSP bypass sequence all complete
without error, and the amplifier registers as an ASoC component.

Add a dedicated compatible reusing tfa9890_init.

Signed-off-by: kschen <admin@kschen.eu.org>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tfa989x.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tfa989x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tfa989x.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tfa989x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tfa989x.c
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 
 #define TFA9890_REVISION		0x80
+#define TFA9891_REVISION		0x92
 #define TFA9895_REVISION		0x12
 #define TFA9897_REVISION		0x97
 
@@ -223,6 +224,12 @@ static const struct tfa989x_rev tfa9890_rev = {
 	.init	= tfa9890_init,
 };
 
+/* TFA9891 is register compatible with TFA9890 for the parts used here */
+static const struct tfa989x_rev tfa9891_rev = {
+	.rev	= TFA9891_REVISION,
+	.init	= tfa9890_init,
+};
+
 static const struct reg_sequence tfa9895_reg_init[] = {
 	/* some other registers must be set for optimal amplifier behaviour */
 	{ TFA989X_BAT_PROT, 0x13ab },
@@ -404,6 +411,7 @@ static int tfa989x_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 
 static const struct of_device_id tfa989x_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "nxp,tfa9890", .data = &tfa9890_rev },
+	{ .compatible = "nxp,tfa9891", .data = &tfa9891_rev },
 	{ .compatible = "nxp,tfa9895", .data = &tfa9895_rev },
 	{ .compatible = "nxp,tfa9897", .data = &tfa9897_rev },
 	{ }
